      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name may come from settlers who migrated from Albany, New York, bringing a piece of their hometown with them.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_Albany%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the mid‑1980s, Les Wexner’s New Albany Company began a master‑planned community that turned the rural township into a suburban hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
